  "guide": "# Workspace memory
/RULES.md contains durable working instructions. Preserve scope words and exceptions. A standalone @notes/name.md includes that note body once; nested imports are not expanded.
/notes/*.md and subdirectories contain Markdown notes with YAML frontmatter: type and description are required single-line strings. Unknown fields and types are preserved. Optional index: false and status: archived exclude a note from the resident index. README.md descriptions summarize directories.
Write one fact per note. Its description states the actionable conclusion and conditions, so reading the index alone is useful. Conditions, reasons and evidence for that fact belong in its body. Separate independent conclusions into separate notes.
Use create for new files, append for additions, edit for one exact unique replacement, replace for whole-file rewrites, archive or delete for notes. Read the complete current file before edit, replace, archive or delete. Replace reports removed lines. Rules budgets include imported notes. External changes are discovered before each request.
